## 3. Remotion 9:16 Shorts Pipeline Assembly

### A. Strict Timeline Validator & Remotion Invariants
When assembling vertical `VideoComposition` (1080x1920 @ 30 FPS):
1. **Keyframe Boundary Clamping**:
   - In Remotion and `TimelineValidator`, keyframes must never exceed clip duration in frames:
     $$\text{frame}_{max} \le \text{duration\_frames} - 1$$
   - A keyframe placed at $\text{duration\_frames}$ violates `keyframe.frame < clip.duration_in_frames`. Always clamp keyframe targets with `max(0, duration_frames - 1)`.
2. **Track Separation for Simultaneous Overlays**:
   - Multiple visual elements visible at the same time (e.g. Background Video, Retention Progress Bar, Subtitles, Hook Card, Branding Badge) **must** reside in separate dedicated tracks (e.g., `track_video_main`, `track_progress_bar`, `track_subtitles`, `track_brand_badge`).
   - Placing overlapping visual clips in the same track causes timeline collision errors (`OverlappingClipsError`).
3. **Kinetic Subtitle Phrase Chunking**:
   - Do not display single words independently on screen; group words into rhythmic chunks of 3–4 words ($0.8 - 1.5\text{s}$ each).
   - Apply micro-spring or ease-out scale animations ($0.9 \to 1.05 \to 1.0$) and rapid opacity ramp ($0.0 \to 1.0$ over 3 frames) to maximize visual rhythm without motion blur.

